    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_7ba2f3f08bfbdd9e8018e0d69528a70a01e7cb203f7afd82076f9aeabebd7c9d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The proof builds a single restricted-domain pipeline across the four units: the failure assumption supplies an integral bound that subharmonic averaging turns into an interior pointwise ceiling; Jensen counting and a reciprocal-Dirichlet-polynomial zero detector then bound contaminated blocks, whose excision produces the zero-free set I_3. On I_3, Mellin smoothing replaces the chosen power of F by a finite Dirichlet polynomial with controlled error, so mean-value orthogonality exposes its diagonal coefficient-square mass. The Euler-product estimate supplies a lower bound for that mass, and finite differences compare nearby vertical-line values so that the resulting variation is registered by derivative means.",
